README
------

Vega Strike: Black Paralysis is a lightweight, standalone space simulation
sandbox designed to run against the Vega Strike Engine 0.11.0+ (Assets API Version 3).

Originally conceived by Daniel Aleksandrow as an unencumbered, minimal total
conversion starter kit, Black Paralysis provides:
- A multi-system sandbox universe (`Isaac`, `Calion`, and `Nan`) with celestial
  bodies, dynamic star lighting, and a circular jump point navigation loop.
- A variety of landing destinations: surface spaceports (`Perseverance`), orbital
  commercial trade hubs (`Commerce_Center`), mined asteroid belt installations
  (`MiningBase`), and deep-space refineries.
- A roster of 5 flyable player vessel classes with cockpits, sound effects, engine
  thrusters, and base shipyard dealer upgrades:
  * Llama (Light Courier)
  * Plowshare (Merchant Freighter)
  * Schroedinger (Fast Patrol Interceptor)
  * Hyena (Medium Fighter)
  * Lancelot (Heavy Superiority Fighter)
- Modern JSON configuration architecture replacing legacy XML configurations.
- Embedded Python 3 base rooms, cargo terminals, news services, and mission scripts.
- Automated syntax validation and asset cross-reference integrity test suites.

--- Building, Packaging, and Running ---

Running Black Paralysis requires the `vegastrike-engine` (0.11.0+) binary:

    # Normal startup into the main menu:
    vegastrike-engine -D /path/to/black-paralysis

    # Launching directly via launcher script:
    VS_ENGINE_BIN=/path/to/vegastrike-engine ./scripts/vsuBlackParalysis

    # Launching specific missions:
    vegastrike-engine -D /path/to/black-paralysis mission/bp_campaign.mission
    vegastrike-engine -D /path/to/black-paralysis mission/explorer.mission

    # Asset packaging with CMake 3.22+:
    cmake -B build
    cmake --build build

    # Generate packages (TXZ, DEB, RPM):
    cpack --config build/CPackConfig.cmake -G TXZ
    cpack --config build/CPackConfig.cmake -G DEB
    cpack --config build/CPackConfig.cmake -G RPM

--- Testing & Validation ---

Run the automated validation suites:

    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
    python3 scripts/test_json_syntax.py
    python3 scripts/test_xml_syntax.py
    python3 scripts/verify_asset_references.py

--- System Requirements ---

    * Hard Drive Space (note: to install the game, /tmp must have enough room
                        to extract the data)
          o N/A

    * Absolute Minimum Requirement (read: technically possible, but don't
                                    bother)
          o Processor: Pentium I 200 MHz or Apple G3 400MHz
          o Video card: 3d card with 16 MB of memory (although it will work
                                                     without a 3d card too)
          o Screen color depth: 16 bit
          o RAM: 256 MB
          o Swap space: ???
          o HD: As above.

    * Reasonable Minimum Requirement
          o Processor: Pentium III 500 MHz
          o Video card: 3d card with 32 MB of memory, and HT&L support
          o Screen color depth: 16 bit
          o RAM: 384 MB
          o Swap space: 512 MB
          o HD: As above.

    * "I want to play Vegastrike at a decent speed and framerate" Requirement
          o Processor: Pentium III 800 MHz
          o Video card: 3d card with 64 MB of memory, and HT&L support
          o Screen color depth: 16 bit
          o RAM: 512 MB
          o Swap space: 512 MB
          o HD: As above.

    * 3l337 Requirement
          o Processor: x MHz, where x -> infinity as 3l337ness -> 1
          o Video card: for (long i=0;i<this_year.length();i++)
                            {newCard(i,USD(500));}
          o Screen color depth: 32 bit
          o RAM: 4096 MB
          o Swap space: Real men will hot-plug new memory modules as needed.
          o HD: I mirror Sourceforge.net, can you?

--- Lore and Historical Development Resources ---

Authentic historical lore, design notes, and development assets authored by
Daniel Aleksandrow have been restored for reference:

    * Design & Lore Notes: doc/lore/PLANNING.md
      Details the Arachnis Sector backstory, Ancient drive research,
      the Aeran attack, and planned mission paths.

    * Historical Artwork & Branding: resources/artwork/
      Contains layered GIMP master splash screen source (splash.xcf.bz2)
      and original project logo banners (BP_logo.png, logo_header.jpg, stardrop.jpg).

    * 3D Model Conversion Utilities: scripts/tools/
      Contains original Blender XMESH conversion tools (blend2xmesh.py, xmesh2blend.py).

